  "caption": "Quinn joined a basketball comp, got a sore spot just below the kneecap, and rested for three weeks. Back on court, the pain came straight back.\n\nRest can calm an irritated tendon, but it doesn't make it stronger. Tendons often adapt to load, so a gradual plan tends to work better than waiting it out.\n\nThings that often help: calming holds like wall sits, slow heavy strength work a few times a week, bringing jumping back step by step, and checking how the knee feels the next morning. Meaningful change can take a few months, so consistency matters.\n\nIf the knee swells, locks or gives way, or nothing changes after months of steady rehab, get it assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
